# What EAS Build does NOT need in the archive.
#
# EAS copies the repository, not just mobile/, so everything here is about
# the whole tree. Note it REPLACES .gitignore for that copy: anything left
# out of this file is uploaded, so node_modules and friends are named again
# below rather than inherited.
#
# The reason it exists at all: backend/.claude, backend/.windsurf and
# backend/.agents hold symlinked skill folders, and Windows refuses to
# recreate a symlink while cloning ("EPERM: operation not permitted,
# symlink"), which failed the upload before a build ever started.

# ── The usual ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.git/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
*.env
.env.*

# ── Nothing but the app is built here ──────────────────────────────────
# The server and the website are their own deployments.
backend/
web/

# Finished apps, 400 MB of them, and the pictures for the store listing.
apk/
apk-react-native/
google-play-assets/

# ── The app's own throwaways ───────────────────────────────────────────
# EAS runs prebuild itself, so the native projects are made there; sending
# ours would ship a local SDK path and a machine's build output.
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/

# The signing key's password. The CLI reads it here and sends the key over
# its own API before the archive is made -- it must never travel inside it.
mobile/credentials.json

# ── Working notes, never part of a build ───────────────────────────────
.claude/
.windsurf/
.agents/
system-overview.txt
